    "title": {
      "en": "Blizzard Temporarily Suspending Players with More Bonus Rolls Than Intended",
      "es": "Blizzard suspende temporalmente a los jugadores con más tiradas de bonificación de las previstas"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Blizzard Temporarily Suspending Players with More Bonus Rolls Than Intended...",
      "es": "Blizzard suspende temporalmente a los jugadores con más tiradas de bonificación de las previstas..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ac5616b7077a8.90401963\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">Blizzard has temporarily suspended players who acquired too many bonus rolls earlier today.<br><br>Weekly Bonus rolls <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/weekly-bonus-rolls-now-available-383270\" data-contiguous=\"true\">went live earlier today</a> and for a short duration after the weekly reset, players could complete the quest multiple times to obtain more than one Bonus Roll. There are screenshots of players with 20+ Bonus Rolls in Discord this morning after this went live.<div class=\"markup-table-wrapper\"><table class=\"exclude-units\"><tbody data-markup-content-target=\"1\"></tbody></table></div><div class=\"pad exclude-units\"></div>Blizzard now appears to have issued temporary suspensions until tomorrow for players who have too many bonus rolls, noting that they will be removing all bonus <a class=\"icontiny q1\" data-game=\"wow\" data-type=\"currency\" data-entity=\"currency\" href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/currency=3418/nebulous-voidcore\"><span><img alt=\"Nebulous Voidcore\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_1205_voidforge_fluctuatingvoidcores_green.gif\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"vertical-align: middle;\"> <span class=\"tinyicontxt\">Nebulous Voidcore</span></span></a> from players.<div class=\"quote-box exclude-units\" data-type=\"user\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\">Blizzard Email<span class=\"quote-said-text\"> said: </span></div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Recent activity shows that a user on this account acquired more void cores than was intended. As a result of this activity we have suspended this account until 2026/<wbr>10/<wbr>07.<br><br>Along with this suspension, we have removed all of the void cores that were obtained beyond what was intended.<br><br>Please note that this suspension won't be lifted until the cleanup has completed and our Support team won't be able to assist with this.</div></div>This ban will only last about 12 hours from the email, but players who are banned won't be able to raid tonight.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>Blizzard has temporarily suspended players who acquired too many bonus rolls earlier today.<br /><br />Weekly Bonus rolls <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/weekly-bonus-rolls-now-available-383270\">went live earlier today</a> and for a short duration after the weekly reset, players could complete the quest multiple times to obtain more than one Bonus Roll. There are screenshots of players with 20+ Bonus Rolls in Discord this morning after this went live. <table>While some players completed the quest multiple times manually, there have been reports that certain auto-turn-in addons were able to complete the quest automatically, but we haven't confirmed this directly. </table><br /><br />Blizzard now appears to have issued temporary suspensions until tomorrow for players who have too many bonus rolls, noting that they will be removing all bonus <a href=\"/currency=3418/nebulous-voidcore\">Nebulous Voidcore</a> from players. <br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\"><h2 class=\"heading-size-2\">Blizzard Email</h2>Recent activity shows that a user on this account acquired more void cores than was intended. As a result of this activity we have suspended this account until 2026/10/07.<br /><br />Along with this suspension, we have removed all of the void cores that were obtained beyond what was intended.<br /><br />Please note that this suspension won't be lifted until the cleanup has completed and our Support team won't be able to assist with this.</div><br /><br />This ban will only last about 12 hours from the email, but players who are banned won't be able to raid tonight.</noscript>            \n        ",
